// ==========================================================================
// Creation (contract interface):
//
// Classes and interfaces whose objects the framework creates instead of the program.
// Framework here means any code outside the application program like
// a DI container, a servlet container, a test runner etc...
// ==========================================================================




// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Relation
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------

// A class or interface the framework creates objects of (no "new" in the application program).
// For an interface or an abstract class, the framework creates an object of a class it makes at runtime,
// so the type stands for that class (e.g. a Spring Data repository, a Spring bean with @Lookup methods).
// The engine makes one mock object for it and that object is used whenever the
// framework calls one of its methods or injects it somewhere.
// Its methods without code (those of an interface) return a mock of their return type.
// It doesn't say which constructor runs, which methods get called or where
// the object gets injected. Specs and frameworks say those with EntryPoint and InjectedWith.
// It doesn't say either that the framework fills the object's fields (that's InjectionTarget).
// Spring: @Component (and @Service, @Controller etc.. via meta-annotations), Spring Data repositories
// Jakarta: @Entity
.decl ExternallyCreatedType(?owner:symbol, ?type:ReferenceType)







// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tuples the contract adds
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Always true when another tuple exists, whatever the framework, so specs and frameworks
// don't need to repeat or ever forget them. Each belongs to the owner of the tuple it follows from
// (for a request its whoever injects into the object).


// A class or interface given to a slot means the mock object the engine made for it,
// so it must have one.
ExternallyCreatedType(?owner, ?type) :-
  InjectedWith(?owner, _, _, ?type),
  ( isClassType(?type) ; isInterfaceType(?type) ).


// A constructor only runs when an object of exactly its class is created
// (with new or reflection), so if the framework calls it, it creates the object.
ExternallyCreatedType(?owner, ?class) :-
  EntryPoint(?owner, ?ctor),
  ConstructorOf(?ctor, ?class).







// --------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Checks
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------

ContractProblem(?owner, "ExternallyCreatedType", ?type, "Owner not declared") :-
  ExternallyCreatedType(?owner, ?type),
  !Owner(?owner).

ContractProblem(?owner, "ExternallyCreatedType", ?type, "Not a class or interface") :-
  ExternallyCreatedType(?owner, ?type),
  !isClassType(?type),
  !isInterfaceType(?type).
